# Scenario: do colonies form, spread and keep their distance?
#
# One line per server console command. Blank lines and # comments are ignored.
# `@wait <marker>` blocks until that text appears in the server log.
#
# Geometry. COLONY_EXTENT is 64 and COLONY_MIN_SEPARATION is 224, so:
#   - two moles closer than 64 to a core join that colony
#   - between 64 and 224 is the unclaimed band: no joining, no founding
#   - 224 or more is free ground
# Group B sits 150 blocks from group A, which is inside the band, and is
# therefore the case that MoleEmigrateGoal has to walk out of. Group C sits far
# enough from both to found on its own.

# 1024 chunks, x -512..511 and z -128..127. The longest emigration walk this
# scenario can produce is about 270 blocks and has to fit inside ticking chunks,
# or the run measures the edge of the loaded area instead of the mole.
forceload add -512 -128 -257 127
forceload add -256 -128 -1 127
forceload add 0 -128 255 127
forceload add 256 -128 511 127

# Nothing may exist yet. Read this in the log before believing anything below:
# a world that was not wiped produces a plausible run that means nothing.
say SOAK-CHECK empty-world
moleverse colony list

summon moleverse:mole -350 -2 0
summon moleverse:mole -345 -2 0
summon moleverse:mole -200 -2 0
summon moleverse:mole -195 -2 0
summon moleverse:mole 250 -2 0
summon moleverse:mole 255 -2 0

say SOAK-MARK setup-done

# 72000 ticks is an hour of game time. Two of them, with a look in between.
tick sprint 72000
@wait Sprint completed
say SOAK-MARK halftime
moleverse colony list

tick sprint 72000
@wait Sprint completed
say SOAK-MARK finished
moleverse colony list
